   priority within that mode.
 - EVERY MODE MUST HAVE AN OUTGOING TRANSITION. A mode block whose body is empty
   (e.g. `} else if (currentMode == FINAL) { }`) or whose transitions are all
-  guarded leaves that mode with nothing enabled. In the extracted Z-machine that
-  is a genuine deadlock: `z_machine Init Ops = process Init (loop (foldr (box)
-  Ops))` loops forever over the operations' external choice, so a mode enabling
-  no operation offers the empty set — `Vis {}`, which is exactly Isabelle's
-  `deadlock`. The generated `<Machine>_deadlock_free` obligation is then FALSE
-  and no tactic can close it (measured: auto OOM-killed at 978s, metis 1825s,
-  blast 922s, fastforce 923s — all searching for a proof of a false statement).
-  A terminal/sink mode therefore needs an explicit TICK-TRIGGERED SELF-LOOP:
+  guarded leaves that mode with nothing enabled, which is a defect in the
+  controller: a reactive controller must be able to make progress from every
+  mode it can reach.
 
-      } else if (currentMode == Mode.FINAL) {
-          if (event instanceof InputEvent.Tick) {
-              this.currentMode = Mode.FINAL;   // idle; keeps the mode live
-          }
-      }
-
-  Use a tick-TRIGGERED self-loop, never a bare `else { currentMode = <same>; }`.
-  An untriggered self-loop becomes a guard-free, trigger-free .rct transition,
-  which the RoboChart CSP generator emits as a tau-self-loop — an autonomous
-  cycle that FDR4 correctly reports as a divergence. A tick-TRIGGERED loop gives
-  CSP a visible event instead, satisfying Isabelle and FDR4 at once.
-
-  What the current extractor emits for such a loop (measured 2026-09-16, not
-  assumed) is
-
-      zoperation FINALToFINAL = ...
-        pre "st = FINAL /\ tick : offered /\ offered <= listens"
-
-  plus an invariant conjunct `st = FINAL --> listens = {tick}`.
-
-  IMPORTANT, MEASURED 2026-09-16: this self-loop is NECESSARY BUT NOT
-  SUFFICIENT. It gives FINAL a disjunct in the deadlock-freedom goal, but that
-  disjunct is trigger-guarded, and the goal quantifies `offered` UNIVERSALLY:
-
-      st = initial \/ (ALL offered_v.  st = READING /\ gas : offered_v /\ ...
-                                    \/ st = ANALYSIS /\ ...
-                                    \/ st = FINAL /\ tick : offered_v /\ ...)
-
-  At `offered_v = {}` every presence-guarded disjunct is false, so any state
-  whose ONLY outgoing operations are trigger-guarded still falsifies the goal.
-  For chem that is READING as well as FINAL. Adding the self-loop therefore
-  removes the "no disjunct at all" defect but not the falsity (tracked as a
-  generator/encoding issue: see thy_generation_rule.egl). Do NOT expect
-  deadlock_free to discharge from this rule alone.
-
-  The rule still earns its place: without an outgoing transition the state has
-  NO disjunct under ANY offer, which is unconditionally false and also breaks
-  FDR4. With it, the remaining obstacle is the offered-quantification, which is
-  a generator matter and not something the Java can fix.
-
-  Modes that already have an event-triggered bare-precondition transition need
-  no self-loop. Do NOT add self-loops to modes with an autonomous outgoing edge:
-  a self-loop there can extend a one-shot tau-step into an infinite divergence.
+  ABLATION (condition D2). The text that stood here explained the mechanism by
+  which such a mode falsifies the generated deadlock-freedom obligation, gave
+  the Java idiom that repairs it, quoted the operation and invariant the
+  extractor emits for that idiom, and stated which modes should and should not
+  receive one. All of that is removed: it tells the developer what shape the
+  PROVER requires, which is the answer rather than the requirement. How to give
+  a mode an outgoing transition, and which event should trigger it, is a design
+  decision for the developer.
 - NAMED BOOLEAN PREDICATES: Before the if-else chain, declare named boolean variables for ALL guard conditions.
   Use descriptive names that encode the sensor/function, reference, and comparison direction
   (e.g., boolean velBelowThreshold = ...; boolean obstaclePresent = ...).
